MID_EV30_016_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_016_m01_001: 'Twould seem multiple gates of the underworld are\non the cusp of our reality.
MID_EV30_016_m01_045: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_046: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_047: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_048: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_049: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_050: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_051: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_052: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_002: Each gate does seem to be more challenging than\nthe last...
MID_EV30_016_m01_003: I fear our enemy is working to disrupt our plans.
MID_EV30_016_m01_004: We suspected they would. This is becoming\na grueling affair.
MID_EV30_016_m01_005: If we are not judicious in how we direct our forces,\nwe may find ourselves out of time and troops.
MID_EV30_016_m01_006: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_007: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_044: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_008: <NCA>"I'll be careful."
MID_EV30_016_m01_009: <NCB>"I'm not sure how to proceed..."
MID_EV30_016_m01_010: <ACA>Good. Our fates are in your hands, so treat\nthem gently.
MID_EV30_016_m01_011: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_014: <ACB>Your hesitance will only instill worry in the others.\nBe bold, even if that boldness is a lie.
MID_EV30_016_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_013: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_015: I have a tidbit of intelligence you might like to know.
MID_EV30_016_m01_016: I've been looking into the temple of the Diadem, and\nI at last understand how to undo the seal upon it!
MID_EV30_016_m01_017: <NCA>"What temple is this?"
MID_EV30_016_m01_018: Hm. Even among her children, few know of\nits existence.
MID_EV30_016_m01_019: The progenitor god, Sothis, created this temple over\n12 thousand years past.
MID_EV30_016_m01_020: I've never heard the name before. What kind of\ntemple are we talking about?
MID_EV30_016_m01_021: Wait, did you say 12 thousand years? That's such a\nlong time ago.
MID_EV30_016_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_023: 'Tis said that any who overcome the temple's trials\ncan gain incredible power.
MID_EV30_016_m01_024: Mind, this was long ago, and the details are scarce.\nBut I'm certain we can win an advantage there.
MID_EV30_016_m01_025: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_026: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_027: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_028: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_029: 
MID_EV30_016_m01_030: Her original landing on this planet was so long ago\nthat your minds would boggle at the thought.
MID_EV30_016_m01_031: She spoke with humans in this land, received their\nworship, and offered them blessings.
MID_EV30_016_m01_032: Then, having seen to the prosperity of the humans,\nshe and her many children began their long slumber.
MID_EV30_016_m01_033: 'Twould have been roughly nine thousand years past.
MID_EV30_016_m01_034: Long before the Great Undoing, yes?
MID_EV30_016_m01_035: Yes. I understand the cause of it was humans waking\nher and provoking a fight.
MID_EV30_016_m01_036: Had they not done so, there is every reason to\nbelieve she'd be sleeping still.
MID_EV30_016_m01_037: Let me see if I understand this. The progenitor god...
MID_EV30_016_m01_038: She guided humans to prosperity and then nearly\nwiped them all out...by accident?
MID_EV30_016_m01_039: The ways of the gods are beyond me. What was she\nmeaning to do, I wonder?
MID_EV30_016_m01_040: Even I am not privy to her deeper intentions. But 'tis\nclear there was some purpose to it.
MID_EV30_016_m01_041: I can at least assure you that the Great Undoing\nwasn't intended to happen as it did.
MID_EV30_016_m01_042: Now then, allow me to mark the temple of the\nDiadem's location on the map.
MID_EV30_016_m01_043: To investigate it will be worth your while—if you can\nspare the time.
MID_EV30_112_m01: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_001: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_002: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_003: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_004: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_005: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_006: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_007: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_008: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_009: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_010: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_011: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_013: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_014: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_015: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_016: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_017: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_018: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_019: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_020: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_021: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_023: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_024: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_025: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_026: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_027: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_028: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_029: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_030: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_031: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_032: 
MID_EV30_112_m01_033: 
MID_EV30_115_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_115_m01_001: 'Tis you again. What brings you here?
MID_EV30_115_m01_002: I was just relaying the current situation to her.
MID_EV30_115_m01_003: <NCA>"How?"
MID_EV30_115_m01_004: Many don't know this, but the souls of Nabateans\nare always tied to her.
MID_EV30_115_m01_005: 'Tis because Nabateans have their origins in the\nsouls that split off from hers.
MID_EV30_115_m01_006: And that is why our souls never participate in the\ngreat cycle, even should we die.
MID_EV30_115_m01_007: When our hour comes, we return instead to her.
MID_EV30_115_m01_008: That said...'tis a tenuous connection. Most would\nfind it hard to notice at all.
MID_EV30_115_m01_009: But as a simulacrum, my soul has much stronger ties\nto hers than normal.
MID_EV30_115_m01_010: Enough so that if I still my mind, I can converse\nwith her.
MID_EV30_115_m01_011: Though "converse" is a strong word. 'Tis more\nfragmented than that term would imply.
MID_EV30_115_m01_012: As I mentioned once, her greatest concern is that\na victorious Balor would seek to go further.
MID_EV30_115_m01_013: Drunk with power, he may choose to challenge her\nphysical form that slumbers in Fódlan.
MID_EV30_115_m01_014: He would lose, for the progenitor god would awaken\nand destroy all the world.
MID_EV30_115_m01_015: Her self-preservation instinct is indiscriminate.\nIt wouldn't stop until everything that moves is gone.
MID_EV30_115_m01_016: That's why she commanded her children, "You shall\nnot wake me up."
MID_EV30_115_m01_017: It has been drummed into us many times that to\ndisturb the progenitor god's sleep is utterly taboo.
MID_EV30_115_m01_018: Once, humans attacked her body where it slept\nunderground, thereby awakening her.
MID_EV30_115_m01_019: Their folly led to the Great Undoing.
MID_EV30_115_m01_020: The simulacrum in Fódlan that housed her seems\nto already be gone from this world.
MID_EV30_115_m01_021: Which means there is no way to keep her in check,\nshould she wake. Unless I went there, I suppose.
MID_EV30_115_m01_022: <NCA>"Are you leaving us?"
MID_EV30_115_m01_023: <NCB>"What is she, exactly?"
MID_EV30_115_m01_024: <ACA>If the need arose, then yes, I would.
MID_EV30_115_m01_025: <ACA>Though even if I went, I'm unconvinced I could do\nanything to control her.
MID_EV30_115_m01_026: <ACA>Her ways are unfathomable to us. She is driven by\nsome purpose we can't know.
MID_EV30_115_m01_027: <ACB>Only she could answer that. All I've heard is that she\ncame from a faraway place in the heavens.
MID_EV30_115_m01_028: Even what we take to be her true body may only be\nanother vessel.
MID_EV30_115_m01_029: And for all we know, one of what we call her vessels\ncould actually be her true form.
MID_EV30_115_m01_030: If it becomes necessary...would you travel to Fódlan\nwith me?
MID_EV30_115_m01_031: <NCA>"Of course."
MID_EV30_115_m01_032: <NCB>"It hasn't come to that."
MID_EV30_115_m01_033: <ACA>If you were there with me, maybe it wouldn't be so...
MID_EV30_115_m01_034: <ACB>True enough. I'm normally not one to get so maudlin.
MID_EV30_115_m01_035: Hm.
MID_EV30_115_m01_036: When the progenitor god first descended to this\nplanet, 'twas not in human form.
MID_EV30_115_m01_037: The people who inhabited this world had difficulty\ninteracting with her.
MID_EV30_115_m01_038: Her true form was incomprehensible to them.
MID_EV30_115_m01_039: All who got even a glimpse of it succumbed\nto madness.
MID_EV30_115_m01_040: All but one, that is.
MID_EV30_115_m01_041: There was a single human who connected with\nher on a deep level.
MID_EV30_115_m01_042: A blind girl, they say—one the humans offered to\nher as a living sacrifice.
MID_EV30_115_m01_043: I'm told that she learned what she knows of humans\nthrough her profound conversations with the girl.
MID_EV30_115_m01_044: The name Sothis itself is said to be what the little\ngirl used to call the progenitor god.
MID_EV30_115_m01_045: As the passage of time carried the girl away, she\ngrieved the loss of her human friend.
MID_EV30_115_m01_046: She made a simulacrum based on the girl's corpse\nand housed her consciousness in it.
MID_EV30_115_m01_047: As for her own body, she hid it away in the land of\nHephthal. It came to be known as a holy site.
MID_EV30_115_m01_048: Afterward, through her simulacrum, she began to\ninteract with humans.
MID_EV30_115_m01_049: She gave them many things, spurring them to\nprosper. And in return, they worshipped her.
MID_EV30_115_m01_050: So it all began. And so today's story ends.
MID_EV30_017_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_017_m01_001: The gate of the underworld should be around here.\nNot that you can tell through this fog.
MID_EV30_017_m01_069: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_070: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_071: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_072: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_073: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_074: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_075: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_076: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_002: Mm? I hear sounds of a struggle. The fighting may\nhave already begun.
MID_EV30_017_m01_003: <NCA>"Then let's not stand around."
MID_EV30_017_m01_004: Exactly so. Let us make haste.
MID_EV30_017_m01_005: We seem to have stumbled upon a clash already\nin progress.
MID_EV30_017_m01_006: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_007: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_008: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_009: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_010: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_011: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_012: Queen Aswan! What do we do? This is a massacre.
MID_EV30_017_m01_013: We can't tell friend from foe in this fog. And the\nenemies, they're wearing our uniforms!
MID_EV30_017_m01_014: Everyone's confused, everyone's killing each other.\nGods! We're all killing each other!
MID_EV30_017_m01_015: Never did I imagine soldiers of Arago would reappear\nas our foes.
MID_EV30_017_m01_016: I need to get my forces to back away, before the\ncasualties mount...
MID_EV30_017_m01_017: But what can I do amidst this chaos?
MID_EV30_017_m01_018: Never fear! There's no one better qualified to rout\nthe armies of the underworld than us.
MID_EV30_017_m01_019: Ah! Might you be...
MID_EV30_017_m01_020: Meet the savior who returned to liberate you all.\nWe've come to destroy this gate of the underworld.
MID_EV30_017_m01_021: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_023: Alright, I'll leave it in your hands.
MID_EV30_017_m01_024: And pray for your safety.
MID_EV30_017_m01_025: <NCA>"We'll take it from here."
MID_EV30_017_m01_026: Soldiers, fall back! May the able assist the wounded.
MID_EV30_017_m01_027: Aswan! Get out of here. I refuse to let you die in\nthis battle!
MID_EV30_017_m01_028: Leda? I'll... I'll go. Thank you.
MID_EV30_017_m01_077: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_067: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_029: Both sides flying the same banners and wearing the\nsame equipment, all in this heavy fog...
MID_EV30_017_m01_030: This was the worst possible foe for Arago to engage.\nAny semblance of order was doomed from the start.
MID_EV30_017_m01_031: New batch of fools come for the gate, eh?
MID_EV30_017_m01_032: Aha. The gatekeeper shows his face.
MID_EV30_017_m01_033: The Promised One, if I'm not wrong! You must be\nquite brave, or quite foolhardy, to stand before me.
MID_EV30_017_m01_034: Now, bow down to the true king of Arago!
MID_EV30_017_m01_035: This gatekeeper is full of himself.
MID_EV30_017_m01_036: Hmhmhm. I like this man. And he does seem to\nbe skilled.
MID_EV30_017_m01_037: I believe you may well make a fine partner in the\ndance of damnation!
MID_EV30_017_m01_038: You know, something about this guy is so familiar...
MID_EV30_017_m01_039: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_040: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_041: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_042: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_043: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_044: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_068: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_045: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_046: 'Tis a cruel irony for a king to threaten his\nown country.
MID_EV30_017_m01_047: A king may do with his country as he will! It is his\nright as sovereign.
MID_EV30_017_m01_048: And I am still sovereign here—there are just a few\npretenders I need to eject.
MID_EV30_017_m01_049: <NCA>"That's not true."
MID_EV30_017_m01_050: You lowlife! You dare voice objection to the mighty\nking of Arago?
MID_EV30_017_m01_051: Foolish man. You're a mere shade now, but once\nyou were the king of this nation.
MID_EV30_017_m01_052: How can you justify dragging your own subjects\nto perdition with you?
MID_EV30_017_m01_053: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_054: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_055: Have you lost even the barest shred of reason in\ndeath? Or were you like that in life as well?
MID_EV30_017_m01_056: In either case, I pity you.
MID_EV30_017_m01_057: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_058: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_059: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_060: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_061: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_062: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_063: 
MID_EV30_017_m01_066: Advance, my armies. Execute these fools for spitting\nin the face of your mighty king!
MID_EV30_018_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_018_m01_001: Mmm. You are...somewhat more capable\nthan I expected.
MID_EV30_018_m01_056: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_057: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_058: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_059: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_060: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_061: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_062: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_063: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_002: But I will not accept defeat. Never! A true king\nknows nothing of defeat!
MID_EV30_018_m01_003: A true king? Yet you were less than I had hoped.
MID_EV30_018_m01_004: I will return. I will! And I will snuff out your breath!
MID_EV30_018_m01_005: <NCA>"That won't happen."
MID_EV30_018_m01_006: There's nothing kingly about such pigheadedness.\nCan't you learn to accept defeat?
MID_EV30_018_m01_007: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_008: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_009: No matter how many times you come for us, we're\nnot losing to you, old man.
MID_EV30_018_m01_010: The insolence. Do you know who you're speaking to?
MID_EV30_018_m01_011: Your opinions will do nothing to sway us from\nputting a stop to Balor.
MID_EV30_018_m01_012: I personally gathered these warriors who overcame\ncausality. Show a bit of respect, hmm?
MID_EV30_018_m01_013: I won't allow you to make light of me!
MID_EV30_018_m01_014: Yes, I see it... You have the same cold shine in your \neyes as she did.
MID_EV30_018_m01_015: I remember her face all too well. The open disdain as\nshe plunged in the blade.
MID_EV30_018_m01_016: Brunhild—Breza's little shrew of a sister—who took\nmy life! As my brother Magor had told her to!
MID_EV30_018_m01_017: Hm. I've heard bards in the north sing about\nMad King Hanno's death.
MID_EV30_018_m01_018: Their songs always suggested his younger brother\nhad him assassinated... Truth in art, I guess.
MID_EV30_018_m01_019: Though if he was as arrogant in life as he is in death,\nit's hardly a surprise he got killed.
MID_EV30_018_m01_020: What? Do not mock me!
MID_EV30_018_m01_021: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_023: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_024: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_025: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_026: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_027: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_028: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_029: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_030: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_031: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_032: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_033: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_034: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_035: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_036: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_037: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_038: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_039: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_040: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_041: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_042: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_043: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_044: Listen well! I am forever the true king.
MID_EV30_018_m01_045: And I will return!
MID_EV30_018_m01_046: What a tiresome man. If I have my way, we'll never\nmeet again.
MID_EV30_018_m01_047: <NCA>"Fingers crossed."
MID_EV30_018_m01_055: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_048: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_049: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_050: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_051: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_052: 
MID_EV30_018_m01_053: It's one nuisance after another with these\ngatekeepers. But I believe our work here is done. 
MID_EV30_018_m01_054: So let's not linger. The sooner we destroy the gate,\nthe sooner we can leave.
MID_EV30_121_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_121_m01_001: Promised One! I thought I might find you here.
MID_EV30_121_m01_002: Allow me to introduce myself. I am Aswan\nHasdrubal Aragon, queen of Arago.
MID_EV30_121_m01_003: I would like to express to you my people's gratitude.
MID_EV30_121_m01_004: Amidst the terrible confusion, I was unable to do so\nthe other day...
MID_EV30_121_m01_005: But you and your allies saved many of my\nsoldiers' lives.
MID_EV30_121_m01_006: And—you destroyed that gate to the underworld.
MID_EV30_121_m01_007: Because of that, we can now shore up our defenses\nthroughout the kingdom.
MID_EV30_121_m01_008: Now, Promised One, I have a request to make of you.\nI would like to be added to your forces.
MID_EV30_121_m01_009: <NCA>"Are you certain?"
MID_EV30_121_m01_010: <NCB>"What about the situation in Arago?"
MID_EV30_121_m01_011: <ACA>Quite. I am resolved to aid you in your fight.
MID_EV30_121_m01_012: <ACA>Before you appeared in Arago, our country was on\nthe brink of destruction. Despair reigned.
MID_EV30_121_m01_013: <ACA>Your arrival changed that.
MID_EV30_121_m01_014: <ACA>Hope has returned. I hear my people speaking\noptimistically about the future.
MID_EV30_121_m01_015: <ACA>Ending this war will mean bringing a measure of\ncomfort to the world.
MID_EV30_121_m01_016: <ACA>That's why I am committed to doing so.
MID_EV30_121_m01_017: <ACB>Arago abounds with highly fortified cities, including\nthe capital, of course.
MID_EV30_121_m01_018: <ACB>There are many citizens taking refuge in such places.
MID_EV30_121_m01_019: <ACB>My kingdom has a long history of domestic\nskirmishes, so cities were built with defense in mind.
MID_EV30_121_m01_020: <ACB>You might say the history of bloodshed has prepared\nus for this moment.
MID_EV30_121_m01_021: <ACB>Arago's fighting forces are considerably depleted\nfrom this war, unfortunately.
MID_EV30_121_m01_022: <ACB>I'm told the army is around three-fifths the size of\nwhat it was.
MID_EV30_121_m01_023: <ACB>It's not as many as I'd like, but it's enough to\ndefend ourselves.
MID_EV30_121_m01_024: 
MID_EV30_121_m01_025: 
MID_EV30_121_m01_026: 
MID_EV30_121_m01_027: 
MID_EV30_121_m01_028: 
MID_EV30_121_m01_029: 
MID_EV30_121_m01_030: <NCA>"I understand."
MID_EV30_121_m01_031: I can assure you as well that I am skilled in combat—\nI've been training since I was young.
MID_EV30_121_m01_032: As one of the hero Arago's descendants, I was\nencouraged to learn the ways of fighting.
MID_EV30_121_m01_033: I'll be all too glad to put my skills to use.
MID_EV30_013_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_013_m01_057: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_058: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_059: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_060: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_061: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_062: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_063: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_064: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_065: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_001: Now, who do you suppose we'll find protecting the\ngate this time?
MID_EV30_013_m01_002: I've heard dismaying things about the settlements\nin this area.
MID_EV30_013_m01_003: They were among the first victims of the underworld\nas the gate here spewed forth its armies.
MID_EV30_013_m01_004: I don't know if I can forgive our enemies.
MID_EV30_013_m01_005: Yeah, they're dead, and Balor's controlling them.
MID_EV30_013_m01_006: We're doing our best to survive, and I don't know\nwho Balor thinks he is.
MID_EV30_013_m01_007: But getting slaughtered just because it makes things\nmore convenient for one side or another is...awful.
MID_EV30_013_m01_008: Agreed, Cai. Your anger is wholly justified.
MID_EV30_013_m01_009: Remember this feeling. Harness it as a cudgel\nagainst Balor, that you might act without pity.
MID_EV30_013_m01_010: I understand that northwestern Brezarant is under\nconstant threat by the forces emerging from here.
MID_EV30_013_m01_011: But Brezarant is known for its strong warriors.\nIt seems to have endured thus far.
MID_EV30_013_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_013: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_014: Mm? Wait, is that...
MID_EV30_013_m01_015: ...
MID_EV30_013_m01_016: That's not possible. Fortuna, what am I seeing?
MID_EV30_013_m01_017: It looks as if the Promised One is standing at the gate\nof the underworld!
MID_EV30_013_m01_056: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_018: <NCA>Attack the impostor.
MID_EV30_013_m01_019: ...
MID_EV30_013_m01_020: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_021: A simulacrum of sorts... Ugh! It had me startled\nout of my wits.
MID_EV30_013_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_023: *sigh* I went to a lot of trouble to make that\nlook like you. And you went and ruined it.
MID_EV30_013_m01_024: Tell me how much you liked it. I'm known as\nan artiste!
MID_EV30_013_m01_025: Well, at least you're here, Promised One. I've run\nout of people to hunt.
MID_EV30_013_m01_026: Hmm... Do I...know you?
MID_EV30_013_m01_027: *gasp* You... You! I remember...
MID_EV30_013_m01_028: Oh, beautiful. I'll pay you back for what you did.\nI'll make it hurt. Hurt good.
MID_EV30_013_m01_029: Hmmm...
MID_EV30_013_m01_030: Uh, Sweetie? You haven't forgotten him...have you?
MID_EV30_013_m01_031: Remember? He was at the tavern when you beat up\nthat other guy and got us into the Heroic Games.
MID_EV30_013_m01_032: Hm. No. I do not.
MID_EV30_013_m01_033: Enough! Don't you make a fool of me! I'll tear you\nlimb from limb!
MID_EV30_013_m01_034: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_035: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_036: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_037: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_038: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_039: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_040: I think it's time to show you just how good I am with\nmy glimmering phantom thread!
MID_EV30_013_m01_041: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_042: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_043: 
MID_EV30_013_m01_044: I'm even more powerful now, thanks to Balor.
MID_EV30_013_m01_045: Everyone who looked down on me had better\nwatch out. They're dead.
MID_EV30_013_m01_046: I'll drag them down to the underworld with me. No\none will escape.
MID_EV30_013_m01_047: Well, well. You're rather arrogant for a dead man.
MID_EV30_013_m01_048: I can see you make a meal out of whatever scraps of\npower are thrown your way.
MID_EV30_013_m01_049: I take it you'll be showing us all what you can do\nwith your borrowed strength?
MID_EV30_013_m01_050: I have nothing left to fear!
MID_EV30_013_m01_051: The Promised One, and the pocket-sized goddess.\nChild's play!
MID_EV30_013_m01_052: Are you...belittling me? Oh, you WILL pay for\nthat one!
MID_EV30_013_m01_053: <NCA>"Leave this to me."
MID_EV30_013_m01_054: Listen to me. Settle the score with this impudent\nhooligan, or I'll be very cross indeed!
MID_EV30_013_m01_055: Go on, then! Make him regret the day he was\nchosen as a Brimstone Lord!
MID_EV30_014_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_014_m01_001: No. No, never. I can't lose. No!
MID_EV30_014_m01_069: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_070: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_071: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_072: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_073: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_074: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_075: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_076: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_002: What is this? With Balor's power? The demon god's\npower? I lost? I can't lose!
MID_EV30_014_m01_003: <NCA>"Yet you have."
MID_EV30_014_m01_004: That's right. Your mistake was thinking that the\npower you'd borrowed was all your own.
MID_EV30_014_m01_005: In the end, beauty is what you lack.
MID_EV30_014_m01_006: Why were you so obsessed with power?
MID_EV30_014_m01_007: Shut up, you little brat. Power is everything.\nEverything is power.
MID_EV30_014_m01_008: It's the only thing that matters. The only thing that\nmakes them listen.
MID_EV30_014_m01_009: I'll never understand that. Why care so much about\nacting that way?
MID_EV30_014_m01_010: Ah... Hehe... Would you just shut up already?
MID_EV30_014_m01_011: You don't know what it's like... To be born into a\nprominent house...
MID_EV30_014_m01_012: Ever since I was a kid, everyone had big expectations\nfor me.
MID_EV30_014_m01_013: But the funny thing is, they just didn't seem to think\nthat much of me.
MID_EV30_014_m01_014: Even that damn Raksha threw me away in the end.
MID_EV30_014_m01_015: And everyone in my house decided I was nothing,\nfollowing my parents' lead.
MID_EV30_014_m01_016: I wish I was never born into that damn house...
MID_EV30_014_m01_017: Does that really matter? This isn't about parents or\nwhich house you lived in.
MID_EV30_014_m01_018: Look at me. My pop was an ex-vulkan. And my\ngrandpa is...Balor.
MID_EV30_014_m01_019: Sometimes my background makes me feel inferior,\nbut I'm basically at peace with who I am.
MID_EV30_014_m01_020: If you blame your whole situation on other people,\nyou'll never be happy.
MID_EV30_014_m01_021: You're the worst. Just be quiet and let me flap my\ngums. My excuses are all I have left.
MID_EV30_014_m01_022: Anything else is just way too depressing.
MID_EV30_014_m01_023: I just want to forget it all! Forget everything!
MID_EV30_014_m01_024: I doubt his resentment has subsided. He may yet\nreturn to haunt our world again.
MID_EV30_014_m01_025: He seemed tormented by his inability to meet the\nstandards expected of him.
MID_EV30_014_m01_026: Though the two were unlike each other in most\nways, perhaps Dyan suffered similarly.
MID_EV30_014_m01_027: Many who gain vast power lose themselves to it\nand succumb to their pride.
MID_EV30_014_m01_028: He is far from the only one tempted by absolute\npower over others.
MID_EV30_014_m01_029: I've no doubt there are more out there who'd eagerly\nbetray the living to join Balor.
MID_EV30_014_m01_030: <NCA>"That's a sad thought."
MID_EV30_014_m01_031: Indeed it is. There will ever be those in this world\nwho crave power.
MID_EV30_014_m01_032: 'Twas true of that Brimstone Lord, but also of those\nwho clung fast to Balor's remains.
MID_EV30_014_m01_033: Their numbers were many, and each may have had\ntheir own reasons. Yet in the end...
MID_EV30_014_m01_034: They were all faced with the same price. Though a\nfew can manage to escape.
MID_EV30_014_m01_035: I'd like to take that as a compliment, but for me the\npower hasn't been easy to resist.
MID_EV30_014_m01_036: Still, I have to rely on it so that I can be of aid\nto others.
MID_EV30_014_m01_037: This is going to sound strange.
MID_EV30_014_m01_038: He mentioned parents, right? That made me think.\nYou seem like a parent to me.
MID_EV30_014_m01_039: I don't just mean my parent. I mean a parent\nto everyone.
MID_EV30_014_m01_040: You let your actions speak for you, and you don't\nneed anyone to understand your reasons.
MID_EV30_014_m01_041: <NCA>"That feels parental to you?"
MID_EV30_014_m01_042: Sure. It's not that you don't care, it's just that you're\nbusy watching over us. Does that make any sense?
MID_EV30_014_m01_043: Kind of reminds me of Pop in a way.
MID_EV30_014_m01_044: Oh my... Heehee.
MID_EV30_014_m01_045: Feelings don't always come across in obvious ways.\nSometimes you have to say what's in your heart.
MID_EV30_014_m01_046: Pop raised me the way he did for my sake, but we\ncould have talked more.
MID_EV30_014_m01_047: It might have made life easier for both of us if he\nwould have just told me how he felt more often.
MID_EV30_014_m01_048: I had to grow up a lot to see all the things he had\ndone for me.
MID_EV30_014_m01_049: <NCA>"Maybe you'll find out what it's like someday."
MID_EV30_014_m01_050: Maybe.
MID_EV30_014_m01_051: I can't imagine myself as a parent.
MID_EV30_014_m01_052: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_053: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_054: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_055: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_056: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_057: 
MID_EV30_014_m01_058: On that note, you're a lot different from what I\nexpected too, Fortuna.
MID_EV30_014_m01_059: Why are you bringing me into this?!
MID_EV30_014_m01_060: There was a shrine to you near Ribeira, where I\ngrew up.
MID_EV30_014_m01_061: So it was normal for folks to worship you there.
MID_EV30_014_m01_062: I never dreamed I'd be talking to you in person\none day.
MID_EV30_014_m01_063: Uhuh. I hope this isn't a roundabout way of saying\nI'm smaller than you imagined.
MID_EV30_014_m01_064: Not at all! You're ferocious! It's just...you're much\neasier to get along with than I thought you'd be.
MID_EV30_014_m01_065: And I feel this parental caring coming from you.
MID_EV30_014_m01_066: It's not just me. Tialla and Peter and everyone else\nwho meets you thinks the same thing.
MID_EV30_014_m01_067: Ah. I, um, I see. That's not so bad a reputation to\nhave, I suppose.
MID_EV30_014_m01_068: But all of this is beside the point, which is to destroy\nthe gate as soon as we can.
